def factorial(n):
    if n == 0: return 1 # Base case
    else: return n * factorial(n-1) # Recursive call|Calculating Fibonacci numbers using a recursive function.

Most primitive types in C, Java, and Python are passed by value by default.|```c
void increment(int x) { x = x + 1; }
int main() { int a = 5; increment(a); // a is still 5 }
```|In Java, when an object reference is passed, the reference itself is passed by value (a copy of the memory address is made), not the object.

```c
struct Person {
    char name[50];
    int age;
    float height;
};
```|Accessing fields: `struct Person p; strcpy(p.name, "Alice"); p.age = 30;`|Classes in object-oriented languages build upon the concept of records by adding methods and access control.

```c
union Data {
    int i;
    float f;
    char str[20];
};
union Data data; data.i = 10; // 'i' is active
data.f = 3.14; // 'f' is now active, 'i' is invalid
```|Unions are often used to conserve memory when storing data where only one type is needed at a time.|When used with a 'tag' or 'discriminator' field, they can form discriminated unions, providing type safety.

